Okay.

01:29:23.800 --> 01:29:38.740
The first one is unstained. That's the first one, right? In the sense that it's getting free of certain seeds for obstacles.

01:29:38.740 --> 01:29:40.740
Here's number two.

01:29:40.740 --> 01:29:44.740
DE DOK DE KHO NA NYID NGON TSIN DU RTOG PA'I YOD ZHIG KYI'I OS ZER GYI RNAM BA DANG BSTAN PO'O

01:29:44.740 --> 01:29:52.740
Aryas, people who have seen emptiness directly, are possessed of the wisdom which perceives emptiness directly, those sun ray lights.

01:29:52.740 --> 01:29:53.740
Sun rays?

01:29:53.740 --> 01:29:55.740
Yes.

01:29:55.740 --> 01:30:04.740
And Yasuji makes a point. He says, I'm not just saying that the truth of the path is the direct perception of emptiness.

01:30:04.740 --> 01:30:13.740
I also want to point out that the JETO PYESHI, the wisdom of the hours after that experience, also account for these light rays.

01:30:13.740 --> 01:30:16.740
The light rays of the sun. The light rays of the sun.

01:30:16.740 --> 01:30:18.740
It's a metaphor.

01:30:18.740 --> 01:30:20.740
Yeah, so that's number two.

01:30:20.740 --> 01:30:22.740
Aryas are...

01:30:22.740 --> 01:30:23.740
They possess...

01:30:23.740 --> 01:30:25.740
Like the sun is possessed by light rays.

01:30:25.740 --> 01:30:27.740
Like that, yeah.

01:30:27.740 --> 01:30:28.740
Yeah, in the end...

01:30:28.740 --> 01:30:31.740
Then there's this huge debate, Michael, if you want to get into it.

01:30:31.740 --> 01:30:35.740
Are the light rays separate from the sun?

01:30:35.740 --> 01:30:37.740
Are they coming out of the sun?

01:30:37.740 --> 01:30:41.740
I mean, is the sun independent of the light rays?

01:30:41.740 --> 01:30:42.740
That's another question.

01:30:42.740 --> 01:30:49.740
Anyway, in the end, it's the wisdom which perceives emptiness directly which destroys the darkness, right?

01:30:49.740 --> 01:30:50.740
And that's why he calls it the sun.

01:30:50.740 --> 01:30:51.740
Okay, third one.

01:30:51.740 --> 01:30:58.740
This is this whole thing where he gets into the six steps, okay?

01:30:58.740 --> 01:31:00.740
With really the last one.

01:31:00.740 --> 01:31:01.740
Which was what?

01:31:01.740 --> 01:31:03.740
Oh yeah, it was like...

01:31:03.740 --> 01:31:07.740
You take all the objects in your life, like things you can see.

01:31:07.740 --> 01:31:13.740
You have some feeling that they must be pleasant or unpleasant from their own side.

01:31:13.740 --> 01:31:16.740
You are looking at them in the wrong way.

01:31:16.740 --> 01:31:19.740
You start to get attachment-like or dislike,

01:31:19.740 --> 01:31:22.740
which is not a real like or dislike, is it?

01:31:22.740 --> 01:31:24.740
And then if you took the opposite of that,

01:31:24.740 --> 01:31:26.740
which is thinking of them the right way,

01:31:26.740 --> 01:31:29.740
that you've made these things that irritate you, right?

01:31:29.740 --> 01:31:34.740
Then we could compare you to the sun of the holy dharma which destroys the darkness

01:31:34.740 --> 01:31:38.740
that lies at the root of ignorant liking and disliking.

01:31:38.740 --> 01:31:43.740
And I would bow down to that sun if I were Maitreya, he says, okay?

01:31:43.740 --> 01:31:46.740
That's how he glosses the three.

01:31:46.740 --> 01:31:48.740
So the third one is that whole stuff together.

01:31:48.740 --> 01:31:51.740
Yeah, yeah.

01:31:51.740 --> 01:31:53.740
Which is really beautiful.

01:31:53.740 --> 01:31:57.740
So the six are really in the third one, yeah.

01:31:57.740 --> 01:32:00.740
Okay, cool.

